{"text":"Next, I want to implement support for file patterns. So, you know how with cursor you can do at file name and it'll inject it into context or add folder and it'll fetch it into context. I want to have something like that. Right? What I want to do is to have two ways of getting content potentially I can we can have like regular filters. I'm thinking something like at f colon file name or at d colon directory path and we can set up like nvim comp for both of those so that we get completion appropriate completions if you pass in a directory hmm if you pass in a directory we crawl all the files in that directory recursively maybe not recursively let's not do okay so I need your help thinking through like what a good app like pattern we can use for including content for the LLM is because what I want to do is to be able to like when I've gotten out the like message pairs I want to just quickly go through the user messages and look for anything that matches these like file like these patterns the query patterns or whatever and then if they're there we do some additional like prompt formatting or something to expand the content to include those those files or folders and so I I like the idea of being able to just add mention a specific file and then that file will get included in that user message in just like the full context maybe just in like a markdown block or an XML tag so that's one one option the other option is like I have this tool I wrote for myself that will parse through a directory that respects gitignore and it will get you you can basically like glob over a folder and it'll print all the files out in XML tags or markdown and it's very useful I'll include the doc string or like the help message for that tool so you can see it maybe just like go over these different options and kind of give me a breakdown of like what you think we could do to bring this functionality into the droid plugin give me a couple different options help me explore this give me different ideas I need you to like put your TJ DeVree's hat hat on right now I need you to be the like NeoVim guru type shit man"}